      "passed": true,
      "tolerance": 0,
      "source": "Orders [6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11] all have t/|omega_n| in [1/5, 5]; the minimum is n = 9 at 0.5770. Recorded as a CAUTION, not a finding: six consecutive orders qualifying means the tower is dense near t, so magnitude agreement here is nearly free and carries almost no information — the entropy bound in a new coordinate. The informative quantity is a_n(Sigma(2,3,5)), not computed here."
    },
    {
